    "abstract": "We present Ru L 3-edge resonant inelastic x-ray scattering (RIXS) measurements of spin-orbit and d-d excitations in exfoliated nanolayers of the Kitaev spin-liquid candidate RuCl3. Whereas the spinorbit excitations are independent of thickness, we observe a pronounced red-shift and broadening of the d-d excitations in layers with thickness below ∼ 7 nm. Aided by model calculations, we attribute these effects to distortions of the RuCl6 octahedra near the surface. Our study paves the way towards RIXS investigations of electronic excitations in various other 2D materials and heterostructures.",
